 succeeded in 0ms:
diff --git a/docs/revision/paper-v2/main.tex b/docs/revision/paper-v2/main.tex
index eb9ac44..f755f8f 100644
--- a/docs/revision/paper-v2/main.tex
+++ b/docs/revision/paper-v2/main.tex
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 \begin{abstract}
 % BEGIN-EV2
 A buyer of computation can check only a sample of delivered jobs, and a sanctioned provider can return at once under a new identity. We show that under uniform audits with refund-and-ban enforcement free replacement makes the ban costless, given honest rivals whose play does not depend on the focal identity. The rule we study, R3, audits new identities first and then keeps targeting the newest ones. In two registered simulation tests, the second locked before six fresh markets were drawn from a Bitcoin block hash, we compare R3 at matched budget and sanctions with uniform audits (B3) and a verified-history comparator, C$^*$. Without honest identity turnover, R3 lowers the attacker's measured gain relative to B3 on every fresh market (the registered replication passes on \site{abs_q4_k} of six), and R3 and C$^*$ are ``\site{abs_q1_cat}'' within a pre-set margin (C$^*$ minus R3: \site{abs_q1_est}); a second verified-history comparator, evaluated without churn, shows no consistent direction. Welfare attacks lower all three rules' gross efficiency to about \site{abs_q3_w0}.
-Exploratory follow-ups after the report locate R3's advantage in the attacker's identity replacement and show that it erodes when honest providers also replace their identities. R3's audits then move to honest newcomers: with the frozen searches, the share of the attacker's jobs it audits falls from \site{abs_ch_fa1} to \site{abs_ch_fa5} between churn rates of $p = \const{0.01}$ and \const{0.05} per round, and at $p = \const{0.03}$ and \const{0.05} both contrasts are lower than without churn on every sampled market. At $p = \const{0.05}$, C$^*$ minus R3 is \site{abs_ch_d5} and B3 minus R3 is \site{abs_ch_q5} (\site{abs_ch_q5d} with the doubled searches). These follow-ups rest on six markets, fixed parameters, illustrative churn rates, one comparator under churn, and searches of which \site{abs_ch_inc} of \site{abs_ch_cells} are flagged incomplete; their market-level intervals mostly include zero.
