 \paragraph{What they do not support.} The selected unconstrained welfare attacks lower the gross efficiency of all three core rules by a similar amount while earning less than the truthful reference against R3 and C$^*$; that is a loss relative to honest play, not necessarily a negative profit. Exploratory mixtures expose policies omitted by the prescribed W1 search that have substantially lower empirical efficiency at non-negative estimated gain; their population profitability remains unestablished, and the favourable W1 result for R3 and C$^*$ is not a lower bound on efficiency. Robustness to the searched families is not established: the doubling checks find missed improvements but cannot bound the remaining gap, and several decisions hold only for the prescribed search procedure. The fresh-market configurations differ from the registered ones in the last binary digit; re-evaluating the frozen policies and references with the registered configurations leaves every Q1 and Q4 decision unchanged, a check that does not repeat search or reference selection.
 % END-EV2
-\paragraph{Limits.} The benchmark is a unilateral deviation against honest opponents; we claim neither equilibrium nor incentive compatibility. At the first-test parameters, Proposition~\ref{prop:terminal} establishes a profitable small same-offer shading deviation in a round with zero continuation loss under every studied rule. Exposure is bounded by the searched families and the optimiser. The fresh markets come from one stated neighbourhood, and the headline market was used in development. R3's registered advantage is measured only when the attacker is almost the only source of new identities. With honest churn the pooled advantage over C$^*$ is unresolved at the two lowest rates and negative from \const{0.03}, and the pooled advantage over B3 changes sign at the highest (Section~\ref{sec:churn}); that follow-up is exploratory, uses illustrative rates and frozen references, runs one verified-history comparator, and leaves the comparison with C$^*$ unresolved at the lowest rate. The comparator was selected on gross efficiency in effect, and the full-budget runner-up left a lower development gain.
